    {
      "sourceId": "src-39b23020e7131b70",
      "quote": "Dr. Sunil Advani A long-time focus of the Advani Lab has been on the understanding and overcoming of tumor radio-resistance. An R01 funded tenured faculty, Dr. Advani and his colleagues have focused on cell signaling pathways involving the PAK-RAF signaling axis. They recently demonstrated that non-canonical, kinase independent functions of RAF mediates cell cycle progression and radio-resistance through phosphorylation of CRAF at serine 338 by PAK. In parallel, the lab is developing tumor-targeted delivery approaches to ultra-potent tumoricidal drugs that have the dual advantage of also radio-sensitizing. Support Dr. Advani’s research is supported in part by a 7-year, $2.5M R-37 from the National Institutes of Health Explore the Lab People Discover the dedicated researchers behind groundbreaking studies in radiation medicine. Meet Our Team Publications Explore the impactful research publications from Dr. Sunil Advani's lab. See Publications Featured Articles Selective Radiosensitization CRAF-Driving Tumor Radioresistance Novel Radiosensitization Approach",
